S("S33A","POLISH","Design review and corrections (the user's list)","VERIFIED",["S33"],
  "A planned pause in the building: you play the finished features as a normal player, write one list of everything you would change or add, and Claude sorts it into small numbered steps before the Options menu (S34) is built.","S34 builds the menu and the Purist-mode proof around the features as they are then; changes made later mean re-doing that proof. This is the cheapest moment for design corrections.",
  "S31 to S33 verified by the user.","PROJECT_STATUS.md; docs/steps/S31.md to S33.md","docs/ only (this step writes no code)",
  ["1. User plays freely for 20-30 minutes (no test script) and writes the list: for each item what they did, what they expected, what happened, what they would prefer, and a priority (must / nice / later).",
   "2. Claude sorts every item into one of four boxes and writes the result in docs/DESIGN_REVIEW.md: (A) tuning of an existing feature (keys, messages, defaults): small fix step before S34; (B) behaviour of an existing feature (like the high-score rule): one numbered fix step each, with its own test; (C) new feature: goes into S34's menu if it needs a switch, otherwise onto the 'after 1.0' list; (D) anything that would change emulated behaviour: refused, or offered only as a labelled Assist that Purist mode turns off.",
   "3. Claude adds the A and B items to the plan as numbered steps (S33B, S33C ...), each small and independently tested, and says what S34 will contain.",
   "4. Claude lists open design questions it noticed itself (for example: settings not remembered between runs, volume control, pad buttons for pause and save, pausing when the window loses focus) and asks for a yes or no on each."],
  ["No code in this step.","Do not change a VERIFIED step's evidence; fixes become new steps."],
  ["docs/DESIGN_REVIEW.md exists and every item is in exactly one box"],"Every correction has a box, a step number or a reason for waiting.",
  user=["Play 20 to 30 minutes freely and send one written list (what you did, what you expected, what happened, what you would prefer, must / nice / later)."],evidence="docs/DESIGN_REVIEW.md"),
S("S34","POLISH","Options menu and Purist mode proof","VERIFIED",["S31","S32","S33","S33A"],
  "Menu for lives, bonus life, difficulty, ghost names (the ROM's DIP options) and a Purist mode that turns every addition off.","Keeps the promise: modern but never silently altered.",
  "Features exist.","src/app/","src/app/menu.*, src/app/main.cpp (wiring, plan change as in S31 to S33)",
  ["Esc pauses and opens the menu; every function key is also a menu item; a side panel lists the keys (S33A corrections).","Purist mode disables overlay, filters, assists, rewind."],["No new gameplay assists beyond a labelled Assist section."],
  ["Replay hashes in Purist mode equal the S27 prototype hashes"],"Identical.",user=["Esc opens the pause menu (the game freezes); use the arrow keys and Enter; Esc goes back; on the main page Esc resumes. Check that each menu item does what its function key does (F1 to F12 still work too) and that the key list on the right matches.","Game options: change lives, bonus life, difficulty or ghost names, choose Apply - restart, start a game and check the result (lives shown at the bottom, bonus life score, ghost names on the attract screen).","Purist mode: switch it on (the game restarts); the greyed items must say LOCKED and the F keys for them must do nothing; play a little; switch it off again.","Close the program and start it again: your menu choices must still be there."],evidence="docs/evidence/S34_purist.txt"),

S("S34A","POLISH","Controls screen: every command with its key and pad button","VERIFIED",["S34"],
  "A Controls page in the menu that lists every command (Up, Down, Left, Right, Coin, Start 1, Start 2) with the keyboard keys and the gamepad button now assigned to it, and lets you change one command at a time.","You see at a glance what is bound to what, and can fix one control without going through the whole list. The key-help panel then shows YOUR keys, not fixed ones.",
  "S32 remapping (F9 and F10 go through every command in turn, with the question in the window title) and the S34 menu exist.","src/app/menu.*, src/app/controls.*","src/app/menu.*, src/app/controls.*, src/app/main.cpp (wiring, as in S31 to S34)",
  ["Menu page Controls > Bindings: one row per command, showing key 1, key 2 and the pad button (names in the game's font: capital letters).","Select a row and press Enter, then press the new key (or pad button): only that command changes. Backspace clears a slot, Esc cancels.","If the key is already used by another command, say so on screen and swap the two (never two commands on one key without telling).","Show the question and the answer inside the picture (not in the window title bar).","The key-help panel shows the current coin and start keys and the movement keys from the bindings.","F9 and F10 stay: they open the same screen. Everything is saved in controls.cfg as before; the file format stays readable by older versions."],
  ["No change to emulated input bits.","No change to what Esc, F1 to F12 do (they stay reserved)."],
  ["Unit test: changing one command leaves the others unchanged; swap on conflict; clearing; save and reload gives the same table","Real-window run on a virtual screen: screenshots of the page before and after a change","Scripted replay hashes unchanged (tests/test_purist.sh, tests/test_replay.sh)"],"All checks pass; the screen shows what the controls file holds.",
  user=["Esc > Controls > Bindings: check that every command is listed with the right keys and pad button.","Change Coin to another key, leave the menu, check it works in the game; then change it back.","Try to give one key to two commands and read the message.","Close and reopen the program: the table must be the same."],evidence="docs/evidence/S34A_controls_screen.txt"),
S("S34B","POLISH","Pad buttons for the menu, pause, save, load and rewind","VERIFIED",["S34A"],
  "Every system command that has a keyboard key (menu, pause, quick save, quick load, rewind) can also be done from the gamepad: the pad can open the menu, and save and load a state, with every pad type.","You can play and use the whole program from the couch with a DualShock 4, a DualSense or an Xbox-type pad, with no keyboard needed.",
  "S34A exists. Today the pad can work the menu only after the keyboard has opened it, and F1, F2, F4 and Backspace are keyboard only (known limitation since S33).","src/app/controls.*, src/app/menu.*","src/app/controls.*, src/app/menu.*, src/app/main.cpp (wiring)",
  ["New pad commands: MENU, PAUSE, QUICK SAVE, QUICK LOAD, REWIND (hold). Default: MENU = right stick click (R3), which every pad has, including an Xbox-type pad made by DS4Windows. The others start unset (the menu already reaches Save and Load by pad); the player assigns them.","The Bindings screen gets one row per new command with the pad column editable and the key column showing the fixed keyboard key (Esc, F1, F2, F4, Backspace); it must still fit the picture.","With the menu open, the pad works it completely: d-pad, A select, B back, and the same pad button that opens it also closes it.","The same rules as the keyboard: Purist mode locks save, load and rewind on the pad too; none of this can change an emulated input bit; coin and start keep working.","Help panel and menu show the pad button for each command that has one.","The controls file gets lines for the new pad commands; older files still load."],
  ["No change to emulated input bits.","Do not use a button that is already Coin or Start by default."],
  ["Unit test: new pad commands bind, swap, clear and save/reload like the others; a button is never on two commands","Real-window run with a simulated pad (SDL virtual joystick) is not possible from outside the program, so the pad event handling is exercised by a small test harness that feeds button events to the same functions","Scripted replay hashes unchanged (tests/test_purist.sh, tests/test_replay.sh)"],"All checks pass; the controls file holds the table the screen shows.",
  user=["Menu: with only the pad (keyboard untouched) press the MENU button, move with the d-pad, choose Save state, close the menu, play on, open it again and choose Load state: it must restore the saved moment.","Repeat with each pad you have: DualShock 4, DualSense and the DS4Windows (Xbox-type) one.","Assign Quick save and Quick load to two buttons you like and use them in a game; hold the Rewind button.","Switch Purist mode on: save, load and rewind must say LOCKED and do nothing from the pad."],evidence="docs/evidence/S34B_pad_system_buttons.txt"),
S("S34V","POLISH","Pad vibration (Xbox, DualShock 4, DualSense)","VERIFIED",["S34A"],
  "The pad shakes at the right moments of the game, with every pad type: Xbox / XInput, DualShock 4 and DualSense (also a DualShock behind DS4Windows). A Vibration option (Off, Light, Full) is in the menu; Purist mode has no vibration.","The game is felt as well as seen and heard: a purr for dots, a thump for a power pellet, a harder thump for each ghost in a chain, a long crumbling rumble at death, and a heartbeat when a ghost is close.",
  "S34A exists. S34B (pad buttons) is waiting for the user's test but this step does not depend on it: it adds its own file and a few lines in the menu and main.cpp. The program never used the pad's motors before.","src/app/menu.*, docs/notes/ram_map.md","src/app/haptics.h (new), src/app/menu.*, src/app/main.cpp (wiring), tests",
  ["A small engine (src/app/haptics.h) reads a few RAM values after each frame (score, lives, level, credits, death animation, power-up, ghost and Pac-Man positions) and never writes to the machine.","Effects: coin tick; a tiny tick for each dot (Full only); energizer thump; ghost thump that grows along the chain 200, 400, 800, 1600; fruit double tap; extra-life triple tap; long fading death rumble; level-done double pulse; soft tick when the ghosts stop being blue; a heartbeat (lub-dub) that gets stronger as a ghost that can hurt you comes within about 28 picture pixels (Full only).","Pad types from SDL: Xbox 360 / Xbox One (also what DS4Windows shows), PlayStation 4, PlayStation 5, other. The pattern is the same; the strength of the two motors differs per type (starting values, to be tuned by the user's test) and the trigger motors are used on Xbox One pads only.","Menu Controls > Vibration: Off, Light (softer, no dots, no heartbeat), Full; kept in settings.cfg; changing it gives a short sample. Purist mode: no vibration. Nothing shakes while paused, in a menu, rewinding, or after a load.","Nothing is judged during the board's power-on self-test (first 320 frames) because the ROM fills memory with test patterns then."],
  ["No change to the emulation: the engine only reads memory.","No vibration without a pad that reports rumble motors; no crash without a pad."],
  ["Unit test of the engine on made-up frames (every effect, the ghost chain, the heartbeat distances, Light, Off, restart, per-type strengths)","Driven run: the S27 replay (7,273 frames, with a recorded real game) plays on a pretend pad of each type (SDL virtual joystick, which records every motor command it gets); counts of coin, dot, energizer, death, fright-end events checked against the game's own counters","Light, Off and Purist runs send nothing to the pad (or less), as specified","Scripted replay hashes unchanged"],"All checks pass; the pretend pads of all four types receive the commands; hashes identical.",
  user=["Plug in your DualShock 4 (cable or Bluetooth), start the game, play: you should feel a light purr while eating dots, a thump on a power pellet, a harder thump for each ghost you eat, a long rumble when you die, and a heartbeat when a ghost is right behind you.","Repeat with the DualSense and with the DS4Windows (Xbox-type) pad. Tell me which feel too weak or too strong.","Esc > Controls > Vibration: try Light and Off, and Purist mode (no vibration)."],evidence="docs/evidence/S34V_vibration.txt"),
S("S34C","POLISH","Controller types, icon and button pictures (Xbox, DualShock 4, DualSense)","VERIFIED",["S34B"],
  "The program recognises what kind of controller is plugged in (Xbox / XInput, DualShock 4, DualSense, or an unknown pad), shows a small icon of that controller type, and shows that controller's own button pictures (A B X Y, or cross circle square triangle) wherever a pad button is shown.","Immediate feedback: the Controls screen says \"Coin: the button with the square\" in pictures, not \"button 4\".",
  "S34A and S34B exist. SDL's game-controller layer already treats Xbox, DualShock 4 and DualSense pads as the same standard pad; this step reads the type and draws the matching pictures.","src/app/menu.*, src/app/controls.*","src/app/menu.*, src/app/controls.*, src/app/main.cpp (wiring)",
  ["Show an icon for the controller in use (a small controller picture with the words PS4, PS5, XBOX or PAD): in the menu header, in the key-help panel and for a few seconds when a pad is plugged in or removed (the user's request, 2026-10-12).","Ask SDL for the controller type when a pad is connected (Xbox 360 / Xbox One / XInput, PlayStation 4, PlayStation 5, other) and say it in the log and in the Controls screen.","Draw the button pictures in code (no image files, nothing copied from anyone): Xbox A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow, LB RB LT RT, View, Menu; PlayStation cross, circle, square, triangle, L1 R1 L2 R2, Create or Share, Options, touch pad; unknown pads: plain names.","Triggers, touch pad and the other extra buttons already bind as buttons (done in the S34B fix); here they only get their pictures (L2, R2, touch pad).","Hot-plug between types updates the pictures at once (unplug the PS4 pad, plug an Xbox pad: the screen changes).","Only one pad is used at a time, as now."],
  ["No change to emulated input bits.","Do not claim a controller type was tested on real hardware when it was only simulated (the user has a DualShock 4, a DualSense and DS4Windows, so all three kinds can be tested for real)."],
  ["Test with SDL virtual controllers set to each type: the right picture set is chosen for Xbox, PS4, PS5 and unknown","Test: trigger and touch pad pictures appear in the Controls screen","Real-window screenshots of the Controls screen for each type","Scripted replay hashes unchanged"],"Right pictures for every type; hashes identical.",
  user=["With your DualShock 4: the icon says PS4, and Esc > Controls > Bindings shows cross, circle, square, triangle, L1, R1, Share, Options pictures that match the buttons you press.","Plug in the DualSense without restarting: the icon changes to PS5 and the pictures follow.","Start DS4Windows so Windows sees an Xbox pad: the icon says XBOX and the pictures are A, B, X, Y (that is what Windows reports; the program cannot see the real pad behind DS4Windows)."],evidence="docs/evidence/S34C_controller_types.txt"),
