S("S37","RELEASE","Publish on GitHub (no ROM)","VERIFIED",["S36"],
  "A clean copy of the project folder for GitHub: no ROM and nothing made from the ROM, full documentation, build instructions, licences, readable code, and a click-by-click upload guide for the user.","Others can read, build and play the project; the user has never used GitHub.",
  "Version 1.0 tested (S36).","docs/DESIGN_REVIEW.md, docs/notes/settings_table.md, PROJECT_STATUS.md","README.md, BUILDING.md, ARCHITECTURE.md, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE, THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, .gitignore, .clang-format, tools/export_github.sh, docs/GITHUB_UPLOAD_GUIDE.md",
  ["Audit: search every file for ROM bytes and for material made from the ROM (the disassembly docs/disasm/pacman*.asm contains the original program's instructions and must not be uploaded; labels and our own notes may stay). Write what is left out and why in docs/evidence/S37_github.txt.",
   "README.md as the GitHub front page: what it is, screenshots, features (all menu options), how to install and run (download the release zip, put your own pacman.zip next to the exe, Windows warning screens), controls and pad, Purist mode, troubleshooting, FAQ, legal notice (no ROM included, not affiliated with the owners of the game, name is a working title).",
   "BUILDING.md (build on Windows and Linux step by step), ARCHITECTURE.md (code map: every folder and file, how the emulator, video, audio and app fit together, how to run the tests), CHANGELOG.md, CONTRIBUTING notes, LICENSE (the user chooses; recommended MIT for our own code) and THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt (miniz, SDL2).",
   "Readable code: add a .clang-format and format src/ and tests/ with it (layout only, no logic change), add a short header comment to every file that lacks one.",
   "tools/export_github.sh builds a clean export folder (no roms/, build/, dist/, zip files, exe files, settings or save files); the exe and zip go on the GitHub Releases page, not in the repository.",
   "docs/GITHUB_UPLOAD_GUIDE.md: click-by-click for a first-time user (create the repository, upload with GitHub Desktop or the web page, write the About text, add the release with the zip)."],
  ["Never include pacman.zip, any ROM file, any file with ROM bytes, or the disassembly with opcodes. No change to behaviour: formatting only, then the full regression and identical replay and Purist hashes."],
  ["Search the export for runs of 16 bytes taken from each ROM file: none found","A fresh copy of the export builds and its ROM-free tests pass following BUILDING.md word for word","README links and screenshots exist","sh tests/run_all.sh and the hash tests after formatting"],"No ROM bytes in the export, the build from the export works, all tests pass and hashes are identical.",
  user=["Follow docs/GITHUB_UPLOAD_GUIDE.md click by click: create the repository, upload the export folder, publish the release zip.","Open the repository page in a private window and check that README, screenshots and download link work."],evidence="docs/evidence/S37_github.txt"),

S("T01","OPTIONAL","Readable rewrite of the game logic (Track B)","VERIFIED",["S36"],
  "Rewrite one subsystem at a time as readable code and prove it matches the ROM over millions of frames.","Only for editable source. Does not change the game's feel.",
  "Complete, tested port.","docs/notes/gameplay_routines.md","src/logic/",
  ["Six pieces, one sub-step each, each with its own step file: T01a random numbers, T01b scoring and lives, T01c dots and fruit, T01d ghost targeting, T01e movement, T01f mode timers.","The shared proof tool is tests/logic_probe.h: it runs the real machine one instruction at a time and compares the readable version with the ROM routine at every call."],["Do not start before S36."],
  ["Each sub-step: side-by-side run (every call compared, memory compared every frame) over millions of frames, plus an exhaustive check of the routine alone where the inputs can be enumerated"],"Zero differences in every sub-step.",evidence="docs/evidence/T01_*.txt"),
S("T01a","OPTIONAL","T01a: Random numbers as readable code","VERIFIED",["S36"],
  "Write the arcade random number generator (ROM routine 2A23) as readable C++ in src/logic/random_number.h and prove it identical to the ROM.","The first piece of Track B; it also builds the side-by-side probe that every later piece uses.",
  "Complete, tested port (S36).","docs/notes/gameplay_routines.md (item 291E), docs/disasm/pacman.asm (2A23-2A34)","src/logic/, tests/logic_probe.h, tests/test_logic_random.*",
  ["src/logic/random_number.h: seed = (seed * 5 + 1) & 1FFF, the answer is the program ROM byte at the new seed; every number named and commented.","tests/logic_probe.h: the machine frame loop with a look before every instruction.","tests/test_logic_random.cpp: a scripted player plays millions of frames; at every call of 2A23 the answer and the seed are compared; the seed in RAM is compared every frame; all 65,536 possible seeds are also run through the ROM routine alone."],
  ['Do not change the game: the readable code is only proved against the ROM and is not used by the game yet (src/logic/README.md).', 'Do not touch anything outside src/logic/ and the new tests (tests/logic_probe.h is the shared side-by-side probe).'],
  ["tests/test_logic_random.sh 3,000,000 frames (about 14 hours of game time): zero differences","The probe loop against Machine::run_frame: identical RAM every frame","Deliberately wrong versions of the readable code are caught"],"Zero differences over 3,000,000 frames and over all 65,536 seeds.",
  user=["Nothing to test by hand: the game is unchanged (this code is not used by the game yet). Tell me OK when you have read the result, and name T01b to continue."],evidence="docs/evidence/T01a_random.txt"),
S("T01b","OPTIONAL","T01b: Scoring and lives as readable code","VERIFIED",['T01a'],
  "Write the score adding routine (ROM 2A5A, points table 2B17), the high score update and the extra life rule (2B33) as readable C++ and prove them identical.","Scoring is the easiest rule to read and check; the extra life rule is used by the achievements.",
  "T01a done (the probe exists).","docs/notes/gameplay_routines.md (items 2A5A, 2B33)","src/logic/, tests/test_logic_*",
  ['Read the routines in docs/disasm/pacman.asm; write src/logic/scoring.h; compare score bytes 4E80-4E82, 4E88 and the lives and extra life bytes at every call over millions of frames and over every points index and every score value that can be reached.'],
  ['Do not change the game: the readable code is only proved against the ROM and is not used by the game yet (src/logic/README.md).', 'Do not touch anything outside src/logic/ and the new tests (tests/logic_probe.h is the shared side-by-side probe).'],
  ["Side-by-side run over at least 3,000,000 frames, memory compared every frame, plus an exhaustive check of the routine alone where possible"],"Zero differences.",user=["Nothing to test by hand: the game is unchanged (this code is not used by the game yet). Tell me OK when you have read the result, and name T01c to continue."],evidence="docs/evidence/T01b_scoring.txt"),
